Yearly or infrequent events

Want to help good articles get better? Sign up for the  [LINK: (February Good Article backlog drive) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Good_articles/GAN_Backlog_Drives/February_2026] ! New and experienced reviewers welcome.

Monthly or continuous events

[LINK: (Monthly contest, WikiProject Military history) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Military_history/Contest] . The contest department of the Military history WikiProject aims to motivate increased quality in military history articles by offering a form of friendly competition for project members making improvements to them. The primary contest available is a simple rolling competition that awards points for improving articles. The contest runs from the first to last day of each month.

Guild of Copy Editors' editing drive.  The  [LINK: (January 2026 backlog drive) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Guild_of_Copy_Editors/Backlog_elimination_drives/January_2026]  is a one-month-long effort by the  [LINK: (Guild of Copy Editors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Guild_of_Copy_Editors]  to reduce the backlog of articles that require copy editing: those carrying the {{ [LINK: (copy edit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Copy_edit] }} tag (also {{ [LINK: (awkward) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Awkward] }}, {{ [LINK: (copy edit section) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Copy_edit_section] }}, {{ [LINK: (inappropriate person) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Inappropriate_person] }}, {{ [LINK: (copy edit inline) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Copy_edit_inline] }}, and their redirects) or are listed on the  [LINK: (GOCE Requests page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:GOCE/REQ] . It began on 1 January, 00:00 (UTC), and will end on 31 January, 23:59 (UTC).

[LINK: (Wikipedia:WikiProject Women in Red) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Women_in_Red]  2025 Events:

Also consider posting WikiProject, Task Force, and Collaboration news at The Signpost's  [LINK: (WikiProject Report) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Wikipedia_Signpost/Newsroom/WikiProject_desk#Sidebar_news_requests]  page.
Please include your signature when adding a listing here.

[LINK: (WP Unreferenced articles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Unreferenced_articles]  is trying to clear the  [LINK: (decades-long backlog of unreferenced articles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Articles_lacking_sources] , please help to lower the number of unreferenced articles below 30,000. Come contribute!  [LINK: (Catfurball) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Catfurball]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Catfurball] )  [LINK: (20:15, 6 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Community_portal#c-Catfurball-20260106201500-Community_bulletin_board]

[LINK: (WikiProject Nevada) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Nevada]  was recently re-activated! New editors interested in the subject are encouraged to join. There are over 800 articles with unknown importance levels. Your help assessing these articles would be appreciated! The sub-project,  [LINK: (WikiProject Las Vegas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Las_Vegas] , has recently become inactive, so new editors for WikiProject Nevada may also be interested joining here!

